d 'MMWS': module to perform marginal mean weighting through stratification
d
d  mmws implements a method, originally proposed by Huang et al
d (2005), extended by Hong (2010, 2012), and further described by
d Linden (2014) that combines elements of two propensity
d score-based techniques, stratification and weighting.  mmws is a
d data pre-processing procedure that reweights a dataset to balance
d the observed pretreatment characteristics across all treatment
d groups. Under the ignorability assumption, the weighted data
d should approximate a randomized experiment. The weights generated
d by mmws can then be passed to the appropriate outcome model for
d use in subsequent analyses. Before using mmws, the propensity
d score for a given treatment must be estimated. A logit or probit
d regression model can be used for estimating the propensity score
d for a binary treatment; an ordinal logit or probit regression
d model can be used to estimate the propensity score for a
d treatment with ordered levels (e.g. varying doses of a drug); and
d a multinomial logistic or probit regression can be used for
d estimating propensity scores for nominal (independent)
d treatments. 
d
d KW: propensity score
d KW: stratification
d KW: weighting
d KW: marginal mean weighting
d KW: causal inference
d
d Requires: Stata version 11
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260915
d
d Author: Ariel Linden, Linden Consulting Group, LLC
d Support: email alinden@@lindenconsulting.org
d
f mmws.ado
